    "body": "I think the two-character encoding will ensure that the snowflake is printed as an emoji instead of a plaintext snowflake. The default config usually uses emoji instead of plain-text symbols. Other emoji in starship that use multi-character emoji also use two spaces to make them render better in most terminals.\r\n\r\nDo other emoji in starship render correctly for you? Is it possible you don't have an emoji font installed? Some terminals will also require more configuration to display emoji: https://github.com/starship/starship/discussions/1600",
