    "updated_at": "2021-06-02T08:59:01Z",
    "body": "Yes, that's what I meant with \"it's still useful\" in my last comment. I'm currently not using emoji fonts, so the character shown is the same with and without the second character (and that's fine for me and not part of the issue).\r\n\r\nAnyway, The string still contains a trailing double space, so the prompt ends up looking something like this:\r\n```\r\n~ via ❄️  pure (shell) ❯\r\n```\r\nwith double space after the symbol. In the PR I removed the double space without touching the symbol emoji.",
